Superpermutation lower bounds

This repository presents general lower bounds, asymptotic comparisons, and
finite refinements from Jay Pantone's superpermutation research. Its sources
are curated from jaypantone/2026-10-superpermutation-bounds at commit
c9ccb6a0d9ddd1007fdce6efab50807ec47464b9.

Seven files in proofs/LowerBounds/ originate from Jakub Halfar's
https://github.com/jhalfar/superpermutations at commit
cc5c763bd5854317b20dadb138990802656e6f03:
SSearch.lean, SCut.lean, SLit.lean, SDec.lean, ChainCapacityC.lean,
SWord.lean, and SSound.lean.

Their source bodies were unchanged in the frozen source repository. This
submission version adds Lean module/public visibility directives and may
contain documented compiler-compatibility changes. The original hashes are
recorded in source-provenance.json. These files supply the window-search
framework used by the ten-symbol proof. The stronger finite certificate and
its connection to the unrestricted word model are supplied by this project;
no numerical improvement is attributed to an unchanged upstream certificate.

Halfar credits Xiaolong Liu's preimage-chain work and the Hunter-Raudvere
library for the background to his framework. His original NOTICE is retained
verbatim in licenses/Halfar-NOTICE. It describes his upstream repository; other
source files and words discussed there are not thereby included here.

Existing source notices are preserved. Retained sources and papers are
provided under Apache License 2.0. Mathlib and Lean are external dependencies
with their own notices and licenses.
